---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../components/GradientText.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Ads Development | Aniloom Technologies" description="Playable ad concept, game design, HTML5/WebGL development, creative production, QA, and release readiness from Aniloom Technologies.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Playable Ads Development</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>A playable is not a small game. It is a <GradientText>focused product.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>We build compact interactive creatives around a campaign goal, a clear delivery specification, and the behavior the experience needs to create.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a playable</button><a class="text-link" href="#scope">See possible scope <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="service-intro section-shell section-pad" id="scope">
      <div class="service-intro__statement" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">One connected delivery</p><h2>Creative intent, implementation, and release constraints have to work together.</h2></div>
      <div class="service-scope-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>01</span><h3>Shape the idea</h3><p>Concept, game design, interaction flow, and the role the playable should perform within the campaign.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>02</span><h3>Build the experience</h3><p>HTML5/WebGL development with UI, 2D or 3D assets, and animation selected for the scope.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>03</span><h3>Prepare the release</h3><p>Variants, localization, click-through behavior, analytics requirements, network adaptation, and final QA as agreed.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Aniloom Playable Quality System</p><h2>Development and QA share the same product view.</h2></div><p>The system connects implementation with layout, scale, typography, responsive states, visual hierarchy, and the end-user journey.</p></div>
        <div class="system-flow" data-reveal><span>Intent</span><i></i><span>Build</span><i></i><span>Review</span><i></i><span>Retest</span><i></i><span>Release</span></div>
        <p class="system-note" data-reveal>This is a working Aniloom method and internal workflow, not a claim of guaranteed campaign performance or external certification.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverable section-shell section-pad">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Scope boundaries</p><h2>What gets defined before production.</h2></div><p>A good playable brief removes ambiguity before it turns into revisions or release risk.</p></div>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div data-reveal><span>Format</span><p>File or package requirements, file-size limits, orientation, platform, and ad-network rules.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Behavior</span><p>Core interaction, call to action, click-through links, end card, and analytics events.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Production</span><p>Assets, source files, variants, localization, review rounds, and responsibilities.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Release</span><p>Target environments, acceptance criteria, test evidence, known limitations, and handoff.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="callout section-shell section-pad" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Start with the campaign goal</p><h2>Tell us what the playable needs to accomplish.</h2><p>We will help define the useful scope, delivery constraints, and next production decision.</p><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a playable</button></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
